tps://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T07:15:27Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T07:15:27Z","body":"as a game dev and creator of game UI’s of 14 years now, i can wholeheartedly say I need autofocus when the node becomes visible; not when it is initialized. it is unclear to whether that’s what this PR does, and I am indifferent to what the variable is called, but that is the functionality I have built for every project time and time again.\r\n\r\nexample usecase: a panel enables a previously hidden sub-panel, so focus needs to move there.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924560086/reactions","total_count":8,"+1":8,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924750909","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106985#issuecomment-2924750909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106985","id":2924750909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uVCg9","user":{"login":"gmikhail","id":4838367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgzNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4838367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail","html_url":"https://github.com/gmikhail","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T09:15:23Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T09:43:12Z","body":"I implemented autofocus when the control becomes visible, as suggested by @AdriaandeJongh. The accompanying documentation has been updated.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2924750909/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2925418628","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106985#issuecomment-2925418628","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106985","id":2925418628,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uXliE","user":{"login":"gmikhail","id":4838367,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4MzgzNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4838367?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail","html_url":"https://github.com/gmikhail","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmikhail/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-31T16:38:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-31T16:51:42Z","body":"Now all tests have passed successfully.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2925418628/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979688301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106985#issuecomment-2979688301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106985","id":2979688301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xmm9t","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T09:45:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T09:45:49Z","body":"> example usecase: a panel enables a previously hidden sub-panel, so focus needs to move there.\r\n\r\n`autofocus` is not a complete solution for this case, assuming you want the 2 panels to be visible together.\r\nYou can move focus to the new panel, but once it closes, you need to somehow focus the previous panel. `autofocus` does not provide that.\r\nIf both panels are visible, you can navigate focus between the panels. Usually you'd want to avoid it, but changing focus mode involves using code (or some convoluted callback binds), at which point you can focus the new Control manually.\r\nEven if you show only one panel, once the sub-panel is closed, you'd want to go back to the button that opened it, not some fixed button that happen to be autofocus. This again involves code.\r\n\r\nSo unless I'm missing something, `autofocus` has rather limited usage and realistically it can save a couple lines of code. It does not avoid adding a script, like mentioned in the proposal, because you need code at some point to properly tweak the behavior.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979688301/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644337498","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106985#issuecomment-3644337498","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106985","id":3644337498,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZOC1a","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T00:12:37Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T00:12:37Z","body":"This could be made more useful if turned into a enum, with the following options:\r\n- **Disabled:** The default.\r\n- **Grab Hidden Focus:** Focus is grabbed but not shown, equivalent to `grab_focus(true)`.\r\n- **Grab Visible Focus:** Focus is grabbed and shown, equivalent to `grab_focus()`.\r\n- **Grab Visible Focus If Joypad Connected:** Focus is grabbed, but only visible if a joypad is connected, otherwise is hidden. I think the only way to do this now is to use `Input.get_connected_joypads()` to check if anything is there.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644337498/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644370583","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106985#issuecomment-3644370583","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106985","id":3644370583,"node_id":"